  "_fallback": "A matched facet is hard: a wood clash only plays a wood sound. When the catalog has none, the first value in this list that has sounds stands in; with none, the engine keeps its own sound.",
  "fallback": {
    "material": {
      "wood": ["steel"],
      "steel": ["bronze"],
      "paper": ["wood", "air"],
      "earth": ["body", "wood"],
      "bronze": ["steel"]
    }
  },
  "_events": "Each engine event kind becomes a catalog request. need: a facet value the sound must have. prefer: facet values that score a bonus. match: event fields that are facets (event.material = 'wood' asks for material=wood). targets: a measured attribute (0..1) the sound should sit close to, computed from an event field ('from') mapped from its range ('in') to the attribute's range ('out'), with a weight ('w'). minDur: shortest usable sound. align: 'peak' puts the sound's loudest 5 ms on the event's moment (a whoosh); 'onset' puts the moment it first comes within 6 dB of its loudest there (a hit, whose top a limiter flattens and whose loudest 5 ms is just one crest of a low wave). tools/sonic_verify.mjs judges a finished mix the same way. variety: how many of the latest picks of this kind are avoided. margin (default 0.15): how far below the best score a sound may be and still be chosen for variety. words (default [kind]): a sound whose name contains one of them gets a bonus. avoid: facet values a sound must NOT have (the physical events avoid synthetic and UI sounds from the Earshot bank).",
  "events": {
